--- ISSUE (description of the bug) ---

number: 1723

title: [BUG] error resetting short-term memory

body (full text, not truncated):

### Description

A disk I/O error occurs when resetting short-term memory

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Create new crewai crew
2. Run `crewai reset-memories -s` or `crewai reset-memories -a`

### Expected behavior

No errors should be raised and a successful memory reset message should be displayed

### Screenshots/Code snippets

```bash
$ crewai reset-memories -a                                                          
An unexpected error occurred: An error occurred while resetting the short-term memory: An error occurred while resetting the short_term memory: disk I/O error

$ crewai reset-memories -s
An unexpected error occurred: An error occurred while resetting the short-term memory: An error occurred while resetting the short_term memory: disk I/O error
```

Long term memory reset is fine:

```bash
$ crewai reset-memories -l
Long term memory has been reset.
```

### Operating System

Other (specify in additional context)

### Python Version

3.12

### crewAI Version

0.86.0

### crewAI Tools Version

0.17.0

### Virtual Environment

Venv

### Evidence

<img width="1237" alt="pyproject_toml" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a56eebcf-abb5-42f6-90ac-155ec13182b3">


### Possible Solution

Inside the `reset` method on `RAGStorage`, call `self.app.reset()` before calling manually removing the folder with `shutil.rmtree(f"{db_storage_path()}/{self.type}")`

### Additional context

None


